{
  // Repo-root placeholder. It compiles nothing and references nothing, by design.
  //
  // This file used to carry `composite: true` plus a `references` array naming
  // all seven workspace projects. Every one of those projects is composite with
  // emit enabled and an `outDir` of `./dist` — but not one of them is actually
  // built by `tsc`: design-system, next-ui and next emit via Babel, next-auth
  // via tsup, demo-v1 via Next. So `tsc -b` from the repo root (which nothing
  // runs, which is why this went unnoticed) would have written a second,
  // competing tsc build over all five of those `dist/` directories.
  //
  // Build order is enforced by `pnpm build:framework`, which runs the packages
  // in the sequence documented in `.claude/shared/dependency-order.md`. Each
  // package owns its own tsconfig; editors resolve the nearest one.
  //
  // The one remaining reference is `next-types`, the only workspace project
  // whose `dist/` really is produced by `tsc -b` — so a solution build here
  // stays safe and meaningful. `files: []` keeps a bare `tsc` a no-op rather
  // than an attempt to compile the whole repository.
  "files": [],
  "references": [{ "path": "./packages/framework/next-types" }],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2023",
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "lib": ["ES2023"],
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true,
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    "noEmit": true
  }
}
